  193: /*
  194:  *  horrible_getputpixel():
  195:  *
  196:  *  This routine gets/puts a pixel in one of the tiles, from the perspective of
  197:  *  the rendering/drawing engine. Given x and y, it figures out which tile
  198:  *  number it is, and then finally does a slow read/write to get/put the pixel
  199:  *  at the correct sub-coordinates within the tile.
  200:  *
  201:  *  Tiles are always 512 _bytes_ wide, and 128 pixels high. For 32-bit color
  202:  *  modes, for example, that means 128 x 128 pixels.
  203:  *
  204:  *  For "linear" modes, y is ignored and x is an offset to select which linear
  205:  *  TLB entry to use.
  206:  */
