 1194:     #  *** RAISED 35 -> 44 BY #513, DELIBERATELY, IN THE SAME COMMIT AS THE FIX. ***
 1195:     #  The six `<arm> ld kill' rows are GONE -- they asserted that a len == 8 READ still
 1196:     #  ends the host at each window, which was true until #513 removed those kills.  They
 1197:     #  are replaced by TWO anchored ACCEPT rows per accepting arm (window base AND last
 1198:     #  slot, because a row at the base tests the near bound twice and the far bound never),
 1199:     #  four CRIME_RE_TEX decline rows, and a 64-bit liveness control.  Arithmetic:
 1200:     #  35 - 6 + 14 + 1 = 44.  Two rows rather than one,
 1201:     #  because a single "35 ok" check cannot tell a LOST row from a FAILING one -- and
 1202:     #  those need different responses.
 1203:     #  *** THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS BLOCK HAD TWO DEFECTS, BOTH FOUND BY THE PASS-2 SEAT.
 1204:     #  (1) It ended in `|| true`, which is INERT: check() in lib.sh has no `return`, so
